# Environment Variable Configuration Template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file to '.env' in the directory you run dead-code-reaper from:
#    cp .env.example .env
# 2. Replace the placeholder values below with your own valid credentials.
# 3. NEVER commit your actual '.env' file or any real secrets to Git.
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. Without any key, dead-code-reaper works fully;
# it just doesn't add AI notes to the report.
#
# When a key is set, `run` sends code snippets of the dead code it found (and
# only that) to the provider, and says so before it does. Use `--no-ai` to turn
# this off for a run.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Model & API Providers (set at most one; Gemini is used first if several are set) ---
# Gemini / Google AI Studio API key (free tier available at https://aistudio.google.com)
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Anthropic API key
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here

# OpenAI API key, or any OpenAI-compatible server (for example Ollama: http://localhost:11434/v1)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# --- Model Settings ---
# Pick a provider explicitly when several keys are set: gemini, anthropic, or openai
# REAPER_AI_PROVIDER=gemini
# Override the default model (gemini-flash-latest, claude-haiku-5-5, or gpt-5-mini)
# REAPER_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest
